Bash(gh pr create --label sandcastle --title "refactor(ocale): migrate universes wire code into domains/cloud-v2" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## Summary

Migrates the Universes Resource wire code into a per-shape sub-tree under
`src/domains/cloud-v2/universes/`, following [ADR-022](docs/adr/022-by-domain-folder-layout-for-ocale.md).
This is the second concrete migration under the by-Domain layout (after
#300, which moved icon and thumbnails) and the first one in the
`cloud-v2` domain — the per-shape rule degenerates naturally to per-entity
here, since universes have a unique shape on `apis.roblox.com/cloud/v2/...`.

- Move `builders.ts`, `parsers.ts`, `operations.ts`, `wire.ts`, `types.ts`
  (and their co-located `*.spec.ts` files) from
  `src/resources/universes/` into `src/domains/cloud-v2/universes/`.
  Imports inside those files gain one extra `../` to reflect the deeper
  nesting; otherwise the bytes are identical.
- Rewrite `src/resources/universes/client.ts` to import builders, parsers,
  rate-limit constants, and parsed types from the new Domain sub-tree.
  The Resource folder is now exactly `client.ts`,
  `client.example.spec.ts`, and `index.ts` per AC #1.
- Update `src/resources/universes/index.ts` to re-export the public types
  from `domains/cloud-v2/universes/types.ts` (the `UniversesClient` value
  export is unchanged).
- Update the two callers of the moved files:
  `tests/conformance/universes.spec.ts` and `tests/helpers/universes.ts`
  switch their `#src/resources/universes/...` aliases to
  `#src/domains/cloud-v2/universes/...`.

The wire requests, parsed shapes, and rate-limit operation keys
(`universes.get`, `universes.update`) are preserved end-to-end. The
`./universes` subpath export, bundle size (24.06 kB / 5.94 kB gzip), and
`"sideEffects": false` tree-shaking guarantee are all unchanged.

## Why

ADR-022 establishes the by-Domain layout for `@bedrock/ocale`, with
Resource folders as thin facades that bind Operations from one or more
Domain sub-trees. PR #300 proved the convention against
`game-internationalization`; this PR is the next concrete migration,
moving the cloud-v2 `get` and `update` Operations onto the same
convention. The forthcoming big-bang migration of the remaining
peer-folder Resources (`places/`, `game-passes/`, `developer-products/`)
follows.

Closes #301.

## Test plan

- [x] `pnpm lint` clean
- [x] `pnpm typecheck` clean
- [x] `pnpm test` 4196 pass / 4 skipped
- [x] `pnpm build` clean (publint reports no issues)
- [x] `pnpm gen:example-tests` regenerated, no diff
- [x] `pnpm lint:unused` (knip) clean
- [x] `pnpm mutate:changed` exits 0; no surviving mutants on touched
      `src/**` files (mutants on the moved-but-otherwise-unchanged files
      are caught by the `typescript-checker` plugin)
- [x] Conformance tests under `tests/conformance/universes.spec.ts` pass
      without modification (only their `#src/...` import alias updated)
- [x] Integration tests under `tests/integration/resources/universes/`
      continue to drive the Resource client unchanged
- [ ] CI verifies the same on a clean checkout

🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
EOF
